win32u: a click does not activate a WS_EX_NOACTIVATE top-level window

"A top-level window created with [WS_EX_NOACTIVATE] does not become the foreground window when the user clicks it"
(MSDN, Extended Window Styles). process_mouse_message activated the clicked top-level whenever WM_MOUSEACTIVATE
answered MA_ACTIVATE (DefWindowProc's default) without looking at the flag; the existing Neutron rule covered
SetActiveWindow/SetFocus only.

Lightroom Classic: dragging the Masks panel by its handle "only moves a little then is stuck in place". Traced on
the nested desk: the press on the handle (a child of the panel, ex 08080080 = NOACTIVATE|LAYERED|TOOLWINDOW)
activated the panel -- frame WM_ACTIVATE(inactive), panel WM_ACTIVATE(WA_CLICKACTIVE) + focus -- and Lightroom
answered by releasing the capture its handle had just taken (its own ReleaseCapture, ~90 ms after the press) and
activating the frame again, so the drag had nothing to follow. Now the activation stays on the frame and the click
is delivered as before.

Measured (fresh launch each, same drag): panel (1747,136) -> (1614,233) for a (-133,+98) pointer drag, i.e. it
follows; NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_CLICK=0: it does not move. Menus, the mask menu and Select Subject unchanged.

Kill switch NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_CLICK=0.

--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -2200,6 +2200,28 @@
     return neutron_noactivate_honor_on();
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON noactivate-click (2026-10-15): "A top-level window created with [WS_EX_NOACTIVATE] does not become the
+ * foreground window when the user clicks it" (MSDN, Extended Window Styles). process_mouse_message activated the
+ * clicked top-level whenever WM_MOUSEACTIVATE answered MA_ACTIVATE -- DefWindowProc's default -- without looking at
+ * the flag. Lightroom Classic's Masks panel (ex 08080080, NOACTIVATE) took the activation from the frame on every
+ * click; Lightroom answers that by releasing the capture its drag handle had just taken (ReleaseCapture ~90 ms
+ * after the press, trace) and activating the frame again, so dragging the panel moved it a little, then stopped.
+ * The click itself is still delivered. Kill switch NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_CLICK=0. */
+BOOL neutron_noactivate_click( HWND top )
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+
+    if (!top || (get_window_long( top, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_CHILD)) return FALSE;
+    if (!(get_window_long( top, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & WS_EX_NOACTIVATE)) return FALSE;
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_CLICK" );
+        on = e ? (e[0] != '0') : 1;
+        ERR( "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_CLICK = %d (%s)\n", on, e ? "environment" : "default" );
+    }
+    return on;
+}
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *           NtUserSetActiveWindow    (win32u.@)
  */
--- a/dlls/win32u/message.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/message.c
@@ -2850,6 +2850,7 @@
                     /* fall through */
                 case MA_ACTIVATE:
                 case 0:
+                    if (neutron_noactivate_click( hwndTop )) break;  /* NEUTRON: a WS_EX_NOACTIVATE top-level */
                     if (!set_foreground_window( hwndTop, TRUE, FALSE )) eat_msg = TRUE;
                     break;
                 default:
--- a/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
+++ b/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@
 extern BOOL is_mouse_in_pointer_enabled( HWND hwnd );
 extern HWND get_active_window(void);
 extern HWND get_capture(void);
+extern BOOL neutron_noactivate_click( HWND top );
 extern HWND get_focus(void);
 extern DWORD get_input_state(void);
 extern DWORD get_last_input_time(void);
